### Manual bad-channel review

A structured sample of Standard, Pitch Deviant, and Duration Deviant trials was inspected visually in SPM. The decision rule was to mark a channel bad if it appeared abnormal in approximately 50% of inspected trials and appeared across more than one condition type, while allowing judgement for channels that repeatedly affected deviant trials.

| Condition | Inspected trials | Main abnormal channels observed | Interpretation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Standard | 1, 208, 417, 625, 831, 1039, 1246 | `MEG1821` on trial 1. `MEG2131`, `MEG2541`, `MEG2511`, and `MEG2331` appeared only on trial 208. | `MEG1821` considered relevant; the other channels were treated as one-off standard-only observations. |
| Pitch Deviant | 4, 391, 928, 1243 | `MEG1821` on trials 928 and 1243. | Supports marking `MEG1821` because it recurred in deviant trials. |
| Duration Deviant | 24, 416, 787, 1238 | `MEG1821` on trials 24, 787, and 1238. | Supports marking `MEG1821` because it recurred in another deviant condition. |

Initial and final bad-channel decision:

```text
MEG1821
```

Channels `MEG2131`, `MEG2541`, `MEG2511`, and `MEG2331` were not marked bad because they appeared only once in a Standard trial and did not recur across conditions.

### Artefact-threshold calibration

After saving `MEG1821` as bad, the maximum absolute trial amplitude was calculated across the remaining good MEG channels. The threshold was selected using the current standardised rule: approximately the 97.5th percentile of maximum absolute trial amplitude.

| Candidate threshold | Rejected trials | Rejected percentage | Decision |
|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 9696 | 62 / 1246 | 4.98% | Too liberal. |
| 12427 | 31 / 1246 | 2.49% | Selected 97.5th percentile threshold. |
| 21912 | 12 / 1246 | 0.96% | Too conservative. |
| 40536 | 6 / 1246 | 0.48% | Too conservative. |

Selected threshold:

```text
12427
```

### Artefact rejection result

Artefact rejection was run using SPM `threshchan`, with `badchanthresh = 0.2`, `append = true`, and a 400 ms excision window.

| Condition | Total trials | Bad trials | Good trials |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Standard | 998 | 25 | 973 |
| Pitch Deviant | 123 | 4 | 119 |
| Duration Deviant | 125 | 2 | 123 |
| Total | 1246 | 31 | 1215 |

Overall rejection rate: 31 / 1246 trials = 2.49%.

### Robust averaging

Robust averaging was run by condition using the established project settings:

```text
S.robust.ks = 3
S.robust.bycondition = 1
S.robust.savew = 1
S.removebad = 1
S.plv = 0
S.prefix = 'm'
```

